# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#   Local development:  copy it to a file named  .env  in this same folder (next to package.json), then fill in
#                       what you need. The server reads .env automatically when it starts.
#   Hosting (Render, Railway, VPS...):  set these in the host's dashboard instead. Do not commit real values.
# .env is listed in .gitignore, so it will not be pushed to Git. Never paste real keys into this example file.

# ---- Core (production only: leave commented out for local development) --------------------------------------
#NODE_ENV=production
#PORT=4000
# required in production
#JWT_SECRET=put-a-long-random-string-here
# put the database on a persistent disk
#DB_FILE=/data/saath.db

# ---- AI chatbot (BACKEND ONLY: these are never sent to the browser) ---------------------------------------------
# With a key, the assistant uses Claude (any language, free-form). Without it, the built-in
# Hindi / English / Hinglish answers are used, so the chat always works.
# from console.anthropic.com > API keys (starts with sk-ant-)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# any current Claude model id; haiku is fastest and cheapest
CHAT_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# how long to wait for Claude before using built-in answers
#CHAT_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
# cost safety cap on Claude calls for the whole site
#CHAT_AI_MAX_PER_HOUR=500
# the contact address the assistant may mention (uncomment and set your real one; if unset it uses the same default as the Policies page)
#SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@yourdomain.in

# ---- Online payments (Razorpay). Leave empty to offer "pay after service" only. ------------------------------
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# same secret you set in Razorpay > Webhooks
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Only for the client build (shown on the policies page). Vite reads this from client/.env, not from this file.
#VITE_SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@yourdomain.in

# ---- Service partners. Leave unset to get safe defaults (see README: "Environment switches"). ---------------
# In production, new partners wait for admin approval and demo shortcuts are off.
#PROVIDER_AUTO_APPROVE=0
#ALLOW_DEMO_PROVIDERS=0
#ALLOW_EARLY_COMPLETE=0

# ---- Alerts and password codes (WhatsApp, SMS, email) --------------------------------------------------------
# Leave any of these empty and that channel is simply off: in development the message is printed in the
# server console instead, in production it is recorded as "skipped" (see README: "Notifications").
# used for the links inside messages (your real domain in production)
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
# one Twilio account sends both SMS and WhatsApp
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# your Twilio number, or a Messaging Service SID (MG...)
TWILIO_SMS_FROM=
# your approved WhatsApp sender, e.g. +14155238886 (sandbox)
TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM=
# email, from resend.com
RESEND_API_KEY=
MAIL_FROM=Saath <no-reply@yourdomain.in>
# The Saath team is told when a new service partner registers (optional):
ADMIN_NOTIFY_PHONE=
ADMIN_NOTIFY_EMAIL=

# SMS for password codes in India (simple, no Twilio). Get the key from fast2sms.com > Dev API.
FAST2SMS_API_KEY=
